    "sha": "b08e38f9ce0ecdb1a5152a52db1ee337348db29f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGIwOGUzOGY5Y2UwZWNkYjFhNTE1MmE1MmRiMWVlMzM3MzQ4ZGIyOWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-15T07:42:22Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-15T07:42:22Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(2d): rest machining on the 2D Pocket operation\n\nA 2D Pocket can cut only what a larger previous tool left (the #1446\ngenerator, machining2d::rest_pocket). The new optional `rest` group\n(previous tool diameter, its corner radius, the stock it left on the\nwalls, the rest allowance) is an operation parameter: changed through\nEditOperationParams (undo and redo restore it), kept in the project\nfile under `rest` (absent reads as off), stamped only when on, and set\nthrough MCP edit_operation (`\"rest\": null` turns it off). Off is the\nplain pocket.\n\nRefused by name at the edit, in the generator's own words: a previous\ntool that is not larger than the operation's tool (when the operation\nis made, edited or given a new tool), negative or non-finite values, a\ncorner radius past the previous tool's radius, the Zigzag and Adaptive\nstrategies, and pre-drilled entry beside rest machining.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/rest_pocket.rs (golden CL\npocket_rest_corners.cl and a reading against the simulated roughing\npass) and operation::rest_op_tests. The page group is a follow-up.\n\nFixes #1489\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
